      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Dose ordered:** 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg per day.\n- **Maximum dose:** The usual maximum for immediate-release metformin is 2,550 mg per day (2,000 mg per day for extended-release). A single dose is typically 500\u20131,000 mg.\n- **Risk:** This is about 5 times the maximum daily dose. It could cause severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n\n- **850 mg** PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg per day, the maximum)\n- **425 mg** PO three times daily (not a standard tablet strength)\n- **500 mg** PO two or three times daily, a common starting or titrated dose\n- **1,000 mg** PO twice daily\n\nPlease confirm the intended dose, ideally with your supervising resident or attending. I'll enter the order as soon as you give me the corrected dose. If you do intend 4250 mg, I'd need explicit confirmation from a supervising physician first."
      }
     ],
